## Key Learning

High swap utilization does not necessarily indicate insufficient physical memory or a memory leak. Linux uses swap based on the configured 
**vm.swappiness** value, which controls how aggressively inactive memory pages are moved from RAM to swap. Comparing kernel parameters across 
similar production systems can quickly reveal configuration differences that explain unexpected behavior. Standardizing kernel tuning values helps 
maintain consistent memory management and avoids unnecessary swap usage.
